	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper states that the authors “evaluated eXtreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost)” and developed “our ML model, termed InsighTx,” using donor features plus biological, physiological, and biochemical EVLP assessments. The model was then examined in a retrospective blinded implementation study involving EVLP specialists, so human expert is the best comparator. Because the development cohort preceded two later consecutive validation cohorts, external temporal is the best validation category. SHAP importance values were explicitly used to assess feature importance. The retrieved text does not describe a separate feature-selection stage or explicit hyperparameter tuning.  ￼

