	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The model predicted EVLP suitability and post-transplant duration of mechanical ventilation; within the extraction framework, the closest postoperative adverse-outcome category is PGD because the paper also linked predictions to PGD grade 3 at 72 h. For the overall model, the best held-out AUROC was 85 ± 3% in test dataset 2. For unsuitable lungs, AUROC reached 95 ± 2%, and for extubation <72 h it reached 83 ± 4%. The paper reports model precision of 81% for identifying any unsuitable donor lung and 72% for suitable donor lungs. For donor lungs predicted to have extubation <72 h, the NPV for PGD grade 3 at 72 h was 88%. Calibration and DCA were not reported.  ￼

